+; chipset (wrong 250/750 timing). The reel is labelled "WS2815 / Data+CLK", but the
+; DATA protocol is plain WS2812 800 kbps; the strip's second ("CLK") wire is driven
+; with the SAME data (see led_utilities.h) so the real DIN always gets a valid
+; signal. **ROOT CAUSE of the whole corruption saga = MISSING COMMON GROUND:** the
+; strip runs off an external 12V PSU; its GND MUST be tied to the ESP32-S3 GND or
+; the data has no shared reference and reads as garbage. 3.3V logic may still be
+; marginal into a 12V strip — a 3.3->5V shifter (74AHCT125) on DATA/CLK is the
+; backup if any sparkle remains.
+; WIRING (bench-reference GPIO map, inherited): DATA pins UNCHANGED from the bench
+; K1 — primary GPIO4, secondary GPIO5. Second ("CLK") wire driven with mirrored
